  "notes": "Module whose defaults (machine_roles empty) create the KMS key, 7 secrets and policies; role, profile and attachment resources are checked as declared. Which policy identifier selects which attachment is not checked (candidates hold the identifier map in locals). Per-policy secret sets are checked through the secret names referenced by a declared policy document (exact set: all listed names and no other resource) or a jsonencode policy (all listed names; for the Consul policy a single-secret resource list). Policies whose documents are built in locals (e.g. for_each over local.policy_documents) cannot be read and fail the policy checks. The three unseal actions are checked separately, so they could come from different policies (single-policy binding needs nested any_of)."
